# Key Takeaways

This lab demonstrates one of the most common file disclosure vulnerabilities.

Although the attack consists of a simple manipulation of a URL parameter, the impact can be severe because it allows attackers to read sensitive files stored on the server.

Path Traversal vulnerabilities often serve as the first step in more advanced attack chains, leading to information disclosure, credential theft, or even Remote Code Execution when combined with other weaknesses.
